# Codex and Claude workflow

- For this project, the user asks Codex to coordinate work and Claude Code to implement it.
- Codex owns scope, exact task prompts, isolated worktrees, independent review, GitHub checks and release verification.
- Delegate to the actual installed Claude Code CLI; do not describe another model or a shared note as a running Claude session.
- Exchange scoped, non-secret checkpoints using the configured `iraniyaragh-handoff` MCP.
- A handoff file alone does not launch an agent. Record the actual worker session/process and state.
- Give Claude a worktree based on current main. Preserve other worktrees and never reset or force-push shared work.
- Claude reports changed files, commit SHA, actual checks, failures and remaining work; Codex checks those against Git and CI.
- Codex handles PR publication/merge and VPS deployment after required checks and successful exact-SHA image publication.
- Production deployment requires the existing lock, fresh restored database/media backups, API-first sequencing and runtime/public verification.
- Never disable checks, dismiss security findings without investigation, or turn uncertain provider outcomes into success.
- Follow AGENTS.md security/data/domain rules. No production secrets, fixture auth, demo seeds, customer exports or fake payments.
- Keep all model sessions and browser artifacts isolated; run heavy checks serially when local resources are constrained.
- Report a failed or unavailable Claude launch honestly; shared MCP access does not imply continuous background supervision.
- This workflow changes when the user's current instruction changes it; it is not authority to expand product scope.
